 "notes": [
  "MY is one unit: assigned wholly to the Federation of Malaya, though Sarawak and North Borneo (most of MY's area) were British colonies until 1963.",
  "ID includes Western New Guinea, still Dutch (Netherlands New Guinea) until 1962; left as Indonesia.",
  "IN includes Portuguese Goa, Daman and Diu (until Dec 1961); left as India. Sikkim (Indian protectorate) is inside IN too.",
  "JP includes Okinawa and the Ryukyus, under US administration until 1972; left as Japan.",
  "PS assigned to Jordan (West Bank, annexed 1950); the Gaza Strip was actually under Egyptian (UAR) administration.",
  "CD assigned wholly to the Congo (Léopoldville); Katanga and South Kasai had seceded de facto in mid-1960.",
  "TZ includes Zanzibar, a separate British protectorate (sultanate); labelled Tanganyika throughout.",
  "MA includes Ifni, still Spanish until 1969; left as Morocco.",
  "NG includes Northern Cameroons, a British trust territory administered with Nigeria until it joined Nigeria in 1961.",
  "VU (New Hebrides) was an Anglo-French condominium; shown under GB_EMPIRE with a label saying so.",
  "Gulf protected states (KW, BH, QA, AE), Tonga, Brunei and the Maldives are shown as GB_EMPIRE though they kept their own rulers.",
  "DE~brandenburg includes West Berlin, which was not part of the GDR.",
  "GB_EMPIRE flag uses the exact Commons file Flag_of_the_United_Kingdom_(3-5).svg (Flag_of_the_United_Kingdom.svg now redirects to it).",
  "Ivory Coast used as the English name for Côte d'Ivoire (the French form became standard in 1985); flag unchanged.",
  "Mali's flag at the end of 1960 still had the black kanaga figure (removed March 1961).",
  "US 50-star flag in use from 4 July 1960, so US is left as itself.",
  "PA includes the Panama Canal Zone, US-administered until 1979; left as Panama.",
  "Malaya's independence (31 Aug 1957) was dropped from the events to stay within 8; MY is still drawn as the Federation of Malaya. Cyprus (independent 16 Aug 1960) also has no event.",
  "Flag-variant polity ids reuse the neighbouring eras' ids: IR_PAHLAVI, AF_KINGDOM, NP_KINGDOM, TIBET, EC_1900, CR_1906, HT_1859 (as 1939/1949); ES_1945, MN_1945, SA_1938, PH_1936, KR_1949, LI_1937, NI_1908, GT_1871, PY_1954, HU_PR, PL_PRL, PRC.",
  "Ecuador (1900–2009 arms), Costa Rica (5-star state flag until 1964) and Haiti (blue-red until 1964) still had their older flags in 1960, as in 1949.",
  "Bhutan's 1956–1969 Commons flag is labelled a possible reconstruction; flags of that period varied.",
  "ZA_UNION uses the dark-colour 1928–1994 file (as 1939's ZA_1928); 1949's ZA_UNION uses the lighter file. Reconcile in the merged file.",
  "Federation of Rhodesia and Nyasaland (1953–63) is shown through its three territories' labels (ZM, ZW, MW) rather than as one label."
